messages "airborne**To: marguskoSubj: IdeaDate: Jan 13Margusko...After our conversation the other day, I had an idea. You seem to be notonly knowledgeable about code, but also able to convey that knowledgein written form.Would you be interested in preparing lessons which we could use to teachpeople new to code how to do so effectively? Each week you could preparea lesson in any format you chose, through posts on your own board, lessonsin a file, etc. Not only would these make for excellent doc files later on, we coulddevelop a testing system which would work well for HM as you go. This would also give you the ability to develop the instruction for the bookyou were planning on writting. By limiting it to a lesson a week it will allow a constructive environment for teaching as many people as possible,especially if you were willing to make yourself available to answer questions during the week.Your thoughts?Airborne**mangla**To: marguskoSubj: Some things to noteCc: sauron kryllDate: Feb  8Well the news has hit the fan. It is well known to the general people whatsome of us have known all along. that you are Leslie. Now, I also hear thatyou will be helping Airborne with the help files. That is definately neededhere.Well, just wanted to drop you a line and let you know that you are notin danger of being removed like you forced us to do Leslie. (If we hadben really worried then margusko would have been gone a while back.)Most everyone deserves a second chance,just use it well. Last of allI know there are ALOT of holes in mud security that we have not plugged.As I told you before I do not want to plug them unless there is no otherchoice in the matter. I would like to trust wizards to know what is right.-Mangla**airborne**To: marguskoSubj: Deadline.Date: Mar  1Hey man.When I spoke to you a few weeks ago, we agreed that you had until the endof Februrary to demonstrate that the project you were working on wouldcome to fruition. Today is March 1st, and I see that nothing has changed.I stood up for you, and probably will again, but I must keep my word andso you have been demoted until you can demonstrate to me that you havesomething substantial to contribute to HM. You can email your proposalto me at airborne@wizvax.net.Airborne**airborne**To: margusko Re:   Deadline.Date: Mar  2I understand man, I am not holding it against you. But I did attach the deadline, and so I have to stick to it. Since all you are doing is readingthe boards, being an Apprentice shouldn't get in the way.Let me know when you have time again, and we can work from there.Airborne**"
